{"answer": "In Spain, for a lease within the compulsory extension, the tenant must tell the landlord, at least thirty days before the end of the contract or of any extension, that he does not want to renew it [1].

In Colombia, to leave at the expiry of the initial term or of an extension, the tenant must give the landlord written notice through the authorised postal service at least three months before, without invoking any cause and without paying compensation [2]. Without written proof of the notice, the contract is renewed automatically for a term equal to the initial one [2].

In Florida, a month-to-month tenancy ends when either party gives not less than 30 days' notice before the end of a monthly period [3]. A rental agreement with a specific duration may require the tenant to give notice before vacating at its end, if it also requires the landlord to give notice of non-renewal in the same period [4]. That period may be no shorter than 30 and no longer than 60 days [4].", "change": "none; the answer states the reference rule with all its conditions, numbers and exceptions unchanged."}
